# nr-office-ooxml-docx-operations: integration fragment

Two modules of the crate mixdog-ooxml (native/core/crates/mixdog-ooxml): docx_tracked_edits (the tracked paragraph rewrite,
the phrase anchor and the tracked find-and-replace at run granularity) and docx_operations (the document-level operations of
the portable Word backend: the table of contents refresh and its measured pages, notes, the document font, style definitions,
page setup, table fitting, content controls, paragraph edits, table cells, tracked-change resolution). No protocol method,
service, Cargo dependency or SERVICE_PENDING name belongs to this task: every crate they use (mixdog-js and
mixdog-ooxml's own modules docx_parts, docx_runs, docx_revisions, docx_formatting, docx_styles, docx_xml, snapshot_docx,
xlsx_audit_support, slide_shapes and xml) is already a dependency or a module of mixdog-ooxml.

## native/core/crates/mixdog-ooxml/src/lib.rs

After the line `pub mod docx_runs;` add:

    pub mod docx_tracked_edits;
    pub mod docx_operations;

## native/core/fixtures/MANIFEST.json

In the "sets" list, after the entry of office-docx-xml / office-docx-revisions (keep the list sorted by set name), add:

    {
      "command": "node benchmarks/rust-core/recorders/record-office-docx-operations.mjs --tree <tree>",
      "fileCount": 1,
      "manifest": "office-docx-operations/MANIFEST.json",
      "manifestSha256": "b24d1f0285929543837fb4a217801bbc9a447df7ecfbea7650cfd7637cc4108e",
      "recorder": "benchmarks/rust-core/recorders/record-office-docx-operations.mjs",
      "set": "office-docx-operations",
      "totalBytes": 436925
    }

(Recompute manifestSha256 and totalBytes from the committed office-docx-operations/MANIFEST.json and golden.json if the tool
that keeps this file reorders or reformats them.)

## For the task that ports portable-docx-edits.mjs and portable-docx.mjs (nr-office-ooxml-docx-edits)

The entry points are the Node exports under their Rust names, all in mixdog_ooxml::docx_operations (operation arguments are the
batch's serde_json::Value, results the result object, errors the message Node throws): refresh_docx_table_of_contents,
write_docx_toc_pages, docx_heading_levels, docx_toc_entries, docx_toc_cache_runs, replace_tracked_paragraphs, add_docx_note,
set_docx_document_font, docx_style_definitions (also what capabilities validates a define_styles operation with),
define_docx_styles, set_docx_page, fit_docx_table, fill_docx_content_control, edit_docx_paragraph (tracking: bool),
style_or_merge_docx_table_cell, resolve_docx_revisions (parts: the document's story and comments part names). The tracked edits
are mixdog_ooxml::docx_tracked_edits::{tracked_paragraph_rewrite, anchor_phrase_in_paragraph, tracked_paragraph_replace}.
Not ported here because it belongs to the dispatcher of that task: the 'an inherited name is not a DOCX operation' test of
portable-operation-names.test.mjs (applyDocx) and the docx comment deletion test of portable-review-fixes.test.mjs
(deleteDocxComment).

## Not compiled

The two modules and tests/twin_docx_operations.rs were written without cargo (the wave is compiled by the lead): the first
build, cargo test -p mixdog-ooxml, is the check (rustfmt parses all three files). The twin test replays
native/core/fixtures/office-docx-operations and needs no Node; twin_live_docx_operations (ignored) re-records through Node.
